WEBVTT

00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:06.070
At one time, gods and demons were as one.

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:09.870
They were sealed away in the abyss of distant memory.

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:14.880
The hearts of humans in fear of the Dark caused this.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.260
For the present, let us call these beings "Shinma".

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.160
<i>Shinma: Japanese for “Gods-Demons”</i>

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:22.790
Now they've awakened and gathered in the Dark.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:28.740
The final night of the gathering, when Shinma and humans met again,

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:34.470
a young girl entered their midst. This is her story. Her name is...

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:43.810
Vampire Princess Miyu

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:54.800
— How about tomorrow, then?
— Sure.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:57.770
Okay, then... the Shijoo Station ticket counter, one o'clock.

00:00:57.770 --> 00:01:00.830
— Don't be late.
— Trust me!

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:05.160
Sorry about before, but don't worry, I'll be there tomorrow.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:06.790
— I promise!
— You better!

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:12.300
Ryooko, are you sure you don't want me to walk you home?

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.040
It's okay. I live really close by.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:16.520
Take care, then.

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:18.220
Yeah. See you tomorrow!

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.880
Episode 1
Unearthly Kyoto

00:01:55.300 --> 00:02:00.130
Excuse me for a moment. Please take your time.

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:01.590
Thank you.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:27.420
The fifth one, right, sir? No blood left in her body.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:30.450
How can something so... ridiculous happen?

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:33.370
Like a vampire... Could that be what it is?

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:37.090
Cut that out. The coroner's looking into it right now.

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:40.010
Don't say stupid things like that again.

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:20.940
Man, it's hot.

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:37.190
Fine...

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:50.610
<i>A rash of vampiric attacks had set Kyoto abuzz with rumour.</i>

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:55.840
<i>I was visiting there on a consultation.</i>

00:03:56.890 --> 00:03:59.800
<i>The request came from the parents of a princess...</i>

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:03.100
<i>who had pricked her finger on the thorn of a rose.</i>

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:08.640
Nezawa

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:14.060
<i>Spiritualist... only one word to cover a variety of activities.</i>

00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:19.260
<i>But those with truly strong spiritual powers...</i>

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:21.770
<i>have a hard time making a living using them.</i>

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:34.750
Heh... garlic.

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:40.170
You say she's slept for 60 days now.
Has a doctor seen her?

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:45.410
The doctors gave her up in the first week as hopeless.

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:54.780
We had an eminent high priest see her, too.
But at that time...

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:57.580
All he'd say was that she had been possessed.

00:05:57.820 --> 00:05:59.550
I see.

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:04.860
<i>Possession.</i>

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:09.460
<i>This phenomenon, usually explained as psychosis,</i>

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:14.410
<i>is still a terror burning deep within the Japanese soul.</i>

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:19.660
<i>But in fact, one rarely, if ever, sees a true possession.</i>

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:22.650
<i>A fox spirit?</i>

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:29.070
She truly is possessed. Allow me to deal with this my way.

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:39.540
This will have to be informal, but...

00:06:59.950 --> 00:07:06.490
I'm sorry. I'll forego my fee, naturally.

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:11.560
Um... I have heard rumours of a vampire appearing in town...

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:12.320
Stop talking such nonsense!

00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:16.310
I saw it! Here it is, middle of summer,

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:19.750
yet someone was near the house, all draped in cloth...

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:20.440
Stop it!

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:22.750
No, hold on a minute...

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:31.700
<i>I may not have to give up on my fee just yet.</i>

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:36.390
<i>My instincts are usually right where money’s involved.</i>

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:44.100
What do you think you're doing?

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:47.000
I'm going to kill the vampire!

00:07:55.400 --> 00:08:00.530
So... your girlfriend was the vampire's...?

00:08:01.430 --> 00:08:04.290
Yeah... its first victim.

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:12.300
<i>Ryooko?</i>

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:20.930
<i>Ryo... Ryooko?</i>

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:29.320
I saw it! The creature, that thing in white,
 went into that house!

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:32.740
Based on that, you think the vampire's in that house?

00:08:33.170 --> 00:08:36.780
It's got to be! That thing's the vampire!

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:39.580
What ran past me that night was the killer!

00:08:41.050 --> 00:08:44.880
If it stays at large, there will be more victims.

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:48.750
I can't let anyone else suffer like I have!

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:51.540
But by yourself, Miyahito... 

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:53.840
To keep that from happening, I've got to kill it!

00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:04.650
<i>Vampiric killings...</i>

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:08.330
<i>The only connection is that the victims were female. Hmm...</i>

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:13.920
<i>A grade school student, junior high student, college student, businesswoman, and housewife... Five in all...</i>

00:09:43.210 --> 00:09:45.530
Fog... inhuman strength...

00:09:45.530 --> 00:09:47.890
glowing eyes... fangs...

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:52.150
Just like the vampires of legend, it would seem.

00:09:54.270 --> 00:09:56.440
But perhaps a bit <i>too</i> faithful to the legend.

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:02.280
I think perhaps...

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:08.740
you shouldn't get any further involved in this.

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:31.940
<i>What was that? It didn’t seem like a little girl.</i>

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:39.860
<i>If Aiko’s the vampire, what’s her motive for those attacks?</i>

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:44.270
<i>For that matter, do vampires really exist at all?</i>

00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:30.120
<i>Vampire!</i>

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:50.370
<i>How can it exist... in broad daylight like this?</i>

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:53.910
Vampire!

00:12:55.760 --> 00:12:57.400
That's what you are, isn't it?

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:02.070
Yes, I am a vampire.

00:13:02.070 --> 00:13:08.260
But, I think, not quite the vampire you think of.

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:13.140
You... You prey even on Miyahito!

00:13:13.420 --> 00:13:21.000
But... it's just what he desired.

00:13:25.270 --> 00:13:25.950
You lie!

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:38.330
If a human desires, I can give him immortality... time everlasting...

00:13:41.490 --> 00:13:47.880
But what we, as well as you, are chasing after is different.

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:52.190
It's only a murderer, capable of bestowing nothing.

00:13:54.090 --> 00:13:59.420
It's just a bloodthirsty... imitation vampire.

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:11.070
Yes... it is Shinma, a being that's both god and monster.

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:16.000
I really don't think you should get any more involved...

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:19.670
Miss Himiko, the spiritualist!

00:14:20.100 --> 00:14:23.590
You have no right to say those things!

00:14:23.990 --> 00:14:26.010
Vampire! Monster!

00:14:26.450 --> 00:14:28.700
People always talk like that...

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:33.930
With clouded eyes and tainted lips,

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:40.240
even though the truth is always within them.

00:14:51.690 --> 00:14:53.780
Miyahito, are you all right?

00:14:58.390 --> 00:15:01.080
Let's go to a hospital immediately.

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:01.630
Why?

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:05.130
"Why?" Don't you know what just happened?

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:08.090
I feel terrific now.

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:12.810
You... you were consumed with grief...

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:14.470
There isn't any now.

00:15:25.010 --> 00:15:26.900
What did you just say?

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:32.630
The car rolled over, with Aiko and her parents inside.

00:15:32.630 --> 00:15:33.780
A roll-over?

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:40.140
We could save Aiko if we operated, but not her parents.

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:45.590
<i>Only, we had none of the AB blood we needed for the operation,</i>

00:15:46.870 --> 00:15:51.510
<i>as we’d already had quite a few emergency operations that day.</i>

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:56.870
Maybe the parents knew that their deaths were at hand,

00:15:56.870 --> 00:15:59.430
because they asked to donate their blood to their daughter.

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:08.770
<i>I had no choice but to accept.</i>

00:16:15.730 --> 00:16:19.500
<i>Aiko’s parents died while she was still on the operating table.</i>

00:16:19.970 --> 00:16:23.520
<i>Does Aiko know about her parents’ blood?</i>

00:16:23.520 --> 00:16:29.130
<i>Maybe. I’m told that she said she was a vampire, at the orphanage.</i>

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:41.180
<i>Stealing her parents’ blood to survive...</i>

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:43.520
<i>If she was berating herself like that...</i>

00:16:57.980 --> 00:17:01.160
<i>...even though the truth is always within them.</i>

00:17:13.310 --> 00:17:16.840
<i>How are her parents here if they’re really dead?</i>

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:22.600
<i>Ghosts? Oh hell!</i>

00:17:33.050 --> 00:17:35.000
<i>The vampire...</i>

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:37.260
<i>The victims were a grade school student, a junior high student,</i>

00:17:37.260 --> 00:17:40.370
<i>a college student, a business-woman, and a housewife...</i>

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:46.580
<i>Women... futures closed off... that would have existed!</i>

00:18:06.760 --> 00:18:08.100
A... Aiko?

00:18:25.090 --> 00:18:26.500
What are you doing?!

00:18:29.320 --> 00:18:31.510
Are you planning on getting Aiko as well?

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:51.730
This is the creature that used Aiko's soul.

00:18:52.250 --> 00:18:54.360
U... Used?!

00:18:54.870 --> 00:18:58.820
In return for providing illusory parents, home, and dreams,

00:19:02.960 --> 00:19:05.460
it drained her of life.

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:29.230
Shinma. A fitting name for those both god and demon.

00:19:29.450 --> 00:19:33.400
One of them – this one – took up residence in her dreams.

00:19:35.210 --> 00:19:39.070
A diseased human soul can easily invite the Shinma in.

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:41.490
Shin... ma?

00:19:44.350 --> 00:19:47.330
Larva, use its true name, and return it to the Dark!

00:19:53.110 --> 00:19:54.330
Ra... en?

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:00.670
Ra... en?

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:03.440
More commonly known as Baku, I think.

00:20:03.910 --> 00:20:05.850
The Shinma who dwells in dreams.

00:20:07.580 --> 00:20:11.140
It uses human dreams as the source of its power.

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:23.320
With its true name revealed, the monster loses its power, right?

00:20:23.730 --> 00:20:25.240
All that remains is to seal it away.

00:21:15.610 --> 00:21:16.970
What about Aiko?

00:21:19.850 --> 00:21:21.090
She's dead...

00:21:21.530 --> 00:21:26.260
Because once possessed by Shinma, human life is forfeit.

00:21:27.170 --> 00:21:30.180
Couldn't you have saved her?

00:21:30.550 --> 00:21:33.600
There was only one way...

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:37.520
but you interfered, remember?

00:21:38.390 --> 00:21:42.440
She could've taken my blood and become a vampire.

00:21:48.880 --> 00:21:55.660
Himiko, I don't know if she'd have preferred life believing that she...

00:21:56.000 --> 00:22:03.630
was the vampire that killed her parents over death. But...

00:22:04.490 --> 00:22:10.450
As for Miyahito... he wanted an escape from grief, Himiko.

00:22:10.900 --> 00:22:14.890
So I gave him his own little world of fantasy.

00:22:15.610 --> 00:22:20.810
He's happier now than he could've ever hoped to be in this world.

00:22:22.730 --> 00:22:25.120
It's true, Himiko.

00:22:25.720 --> 00:22:29.730
Well, bye-bye!

00:22:32.660 --> 00:22:37.580
That can't be! A fantasy world?!

00:23:00.270 --> 00:23:03.630
Hey, get this... I hear he's been like that for who-knows-how-long!

00:23:03.630 --> 00:23:05.370
He's famous around here.

00:23:05.370 --> 00:23:07.280
— He's weird, huh?
— Uh-huh.

00:23:07.280 --> 00:23:10.410
— I know about him.
— What?

00:23:10.410 --> 00:23:12.240
He's living in happiness.

00:23:12.240 --> 00:23:14.060
Huh?! What?!

00:23:14.060 --> 00:23:15.450
What do you mean?

00:23:15.810 --> 00:23:19.370
Wouldn't you like to be able to be happy forever?

00:23:19.780 --> 00:23:24.290
That's weird!

00:23:27.780 --> 00:23:30.390
Let's go. We'll be late for school.

00:23:30.390 --> 00:23:32.340
Yeah, let's go!

00:23:39.510 --> 00:23:44.060
I, a spiritualist who never believed demons existed,

00:23:45.420 --> 00:23:47.490
will hunt down that little devil,

00:23:47.490 --> 00:23:50.990
the vampire girl who vanished without giving her name.

00:23:51.890 --> 00:23:57.840
My happiness isn't trivial enough to be found in fantasy.
